    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d547-a2">

                <pb facs="1301" n="1187" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1187"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2—Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Head of the Planning Staff, Fifteenth Army
                        Group</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Richardson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Chief of the Imperial General Staff</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Brooke</hi>)<anchor n="3" xml:id="d547-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-26">26 <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >August</hi> 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cgs</hi> 53 26 August. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Bigot</hi>. Personal for C.I.G.S. from Eichardson. Ref. 62930 (C.I.G.S.)
                    dated 26 (<hi rendition="#small-caps">Welfare</hi> 423).</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>General Alexander is visiting formations of 5th U.S.A. Army. The slow rate
                        of build up due to length of turn round and limited resources in craft
                        caused some re-examination here. The following steps to speed build up were
                        decided upon at a meeting in Algiers on 23rd August. <list>
                            <label>
                                <hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>.</label>
                            <item>The withdrawal of the craft from <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Baytown</hi> after (? initial<anchor n="4" xml:id="d547-f2"/>)
                                assault, thus giving fullest priority <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Avalanche</hi>.</item>
                            <label>
                                <hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>.</label>
                            <item>The allocation of 45 U.S.A. Division in Sicily to 5th U.S.A. Army,
                                so shortening the turn round from Naples.</item>
                            <label>
                                <hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.</label>
                            <item>The examination of use of 2 U.S.A. Armoured Divisions from Sicily
                                with a view to shortening turn round.</item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>There is no intention to march all <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Baytown</hi> Divisions through Calabria if situation permits them to be
                        sent by sea and the resources in shipping and (? destroyers<anchor n="4"
                            xml:id="d547-f3"/>) make a sea move more profitable.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>I cannot give you now the exact rate of build up we are hoping to achieve
                        but it is considerably greater than that stated by General Whiteley. The Air
                        Force commitment is very large and this has to be set against any
                        requirements in allocating the total lift available.</item>
                    <pb facs="1302" n="1188" xml:id="pg1188"/>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>I will send estimated rate of build up as soon as this has been finally
                        worked out. The build up figure has to be obtained from A.F.H.Q. as so much
                        depends upon loading facilities.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d547-f1" n="3" type="source" xml:id="d547-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to London; forwarded by the Air Ministry to Brooke in Canada in telegram No.
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Concrete</hi> 597, August 27, 1943.</p>
            </note>
